  "notes": "PLAT-01 cycle 2: phenomenon B, the isolated multi-millisecond event, not a figure. Break limit 3000 us, which is T_B derived in cycle 1 from a traced baseline and recorded in docs/rig/plat01-stall-investigation.md. Target is the event family that produced the 3679 to 3806 us per-thread maxima on 2026-08-28. Instrument ordering: (a) sequential, two separate runs, NOT (b) concurrent. (b) would run rtla sampling threads at SCHED_FIFO on cpus 6-11, the same cores this run measures at priority 99, which is what starved 2026-09-06-precision3591-screen-02, and an investigation run records TracersQuiescent NotApplicable so nothing would refuse it. Event set armed by scripts/nr-arm-trace.sh: sched:sched_switch sched:sched_wakeup irq:irq_handler_entry irq:irq_handler_exit timer:hrtimer_expire_entry workqueue:workqueue_execute_start ipi:ipi_send_cpu ipi:ipi_send_cpumask tlb:tlb_flush. tracing_cpumask 3fffff over all 22 logical cpus so an IPI sender is visible and not only its arrival; buffer_size_kb 8195 per cpu. Whether the break fired, and the buffer line counts if it did, are recorded in the plan summary rather than here: this note is written at launch."
